<h2>Harness 100 · Practice Ideas · Performance</h2>

<h3>Harness 100</h3>
<p>A published collection that <strong>composes 100 case harnesses in advance</strong> for the things you need in daily life and at work. (Search for "harness 100"; a Korean version is provided.) The fields are as follows.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Content production (YouTube planning · podcasts · newsletters · online courses)</li>
    <li>Software development, data analysis</li>
    <li>Business strategy (from validating a startup idea to pitching, <strong>government support program business plans</strong>)</li>
    <li>Education · learning, law (risk assessment), health · lifestyle, communication, operating processes, specialized domains</li>
</ul>
<p>For example, "writing a government support program business plan" already comes with agents like a <strong>public notice analysis expert · business viability section writer · budget planning helper</strong> and the related skills. Users make use of it by <strong>finding a similar composition and customizing it</strong>.</p>

<h3>Ten ideas worth practicing</h3>
<ol>
    <li>Paper PDF → one-page summary card</li>
    <li>Experiment data cleanup → visualization → report pipeline</li>
    <li><strong>Patent research</strong> on prior art (backed by strong research)</li>
    <li>Writing a research proposal</li>
    <li>Setting up and verifying a simulation environment</li>
    <li>Refactoring legacy code</li>
    <li>Documentation</li>
    <li>Producing integrated presentation materials</li>
    <li>Writing a national project report</li>
    <li>Research data curation</li>
</ol>
<p>If a site you want to pull from needs an API integration, you can make that itself into a <strong>skill</strong> and connect it to an agent.</p>

